      "content": "The defense's \"standard procedure\" argument is a legal shield designed to protect the actions of the accused, not a factual defense against perjury. When a witness knowingly provides false testimony under oath, the intent to deceive is paramount, and the prosecution's case must be judged against that high bar. Any attempt to frame a lie as mere procedure is a weak deflection that the legal system is designed to expose.",
      "source": "target",
