    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That sounds pretty biased. You're basically saying the defense is just making excuses and doesn't have a valid point. If an expert witness or a government official says something that contradicts the facts, but they claim they were following established protocols, isn't it possible they weren't being deceptive, just following a different set of rules? Why is it automatically a \"weak deflection\" instead of a legitimate context for their testimony?",
